WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
You make contracts EVERY day.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.470
A meal deal.

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.890
A bus ticket...

4
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.190
You just don't notice.

5
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.580
So what turns a chat into

6
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.020
a contract? In Scots law...

7
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.680
SIX things have to line up.

8
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.130
Here's the twist.

9
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.310
The price on the shelf?

10
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.370
NOT an offer.

11
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.790
It's an invitation to treat.

12
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.290
YOU make the offer — at

13
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:28.730
the till.

14
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.020
Then they accept — no changes.

15
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.100
But add a new term...

16
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.660
and it's a counter-offer.

17
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.760
The first offer is DEAD.

18
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.910
You both have to mean the

19
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.730
SAME deal. And you have to

20
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.710
mean it seriously.

21
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.450
Coffee with a friend?

22
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.250
Not a contract.

23
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.340
And you need capacity.

24
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.460
Under sixteen? Only everyday deals.

25
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.060
At sixteen or seventeen — a

26
00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.560
bad deal can be undone...

27
00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.250
right up until you're twenty-one.

28
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.750
Now... one change is coming.

29
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.483
Once a new Act is in

30
00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:14.050
force, an acceptance only counts when

31
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.150
it REACHES the other person.

32
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.760
Parties. Offer. Acceptance.

33
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.240
Agreement. Intention. Capacity...

34
00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.240
That's a contract.
